<< {"id":1,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"capabilities":{"resources":{"listChanged":false,"subscribe":false},"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"instructions":"JETCARP runs cellular automata (the Game of Life and many other rules) on square, hexagon, triangle, Archimedean, k-uniform and aperiodic (Spectre, hat, Penrose) tilings, and keeps a library of the patterns its searches find. Typical flow: world_new (a tiling and rules) -> world_edit (draw or paste) -> world_step -> world_read / world_render. Long searches: search_start, job_status, then library_query for the finds. Call help for worked examples, reference for rule names, tilings, palettes and seeds. The JETCARP book is available as resources (jetcarp://docs/...) and through help {\"page\": ...}.","protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","resultType":"complete","serverInfo":{"name":"jetcarp","title":"JETCARP cellular automata","version":"0.4.2-rc.4"}}}
